DESCRIPTION:Äänen Lumo\, Toinen kerros.\n\nPay-what-you-can 5-15 €.\n\
 nCorinna Eikmeier\, cello\nLibero Mureddu\, keyboards\nLivia Schweizer\, f
 lutes\nIida-Vilhelmiina Sinisalo\, cello\n\nGerman cellist and improviser 
 Corinna Eikmeier (DE) returns to Helsinki to perform with some improvisers
  from the Finnish scene with whom she has previously worked.\n\nProf. Dr. 
 Corinna Eikmeier studied cello and improvisation and is a Feldenkrais teac
 her. She completed her doctorate in Vienna on the subject of “Movement Q
 uality and Musical Practice. On the Relationship between the Feldenkrais M
 ethod and Musical Improvisation”. She has been teaching improvisation at
  the Hanover University of Music\, Drama and Media since 2007. From 2017 t
 o 2018 she was a visiting professor of music education at the Brandenburg 
 University of Technology Cottbus Senftenberg. Since 2020 she has been a pr
 ofessor of instrumental and vocal pedagogy at the Lübeck Academy of Music
 . She specialises in improvisation and currently plays in permanent ensemb
 les including Cellophan and the First Improvising String Orchestra\, and s
 he frequently participates in interdisciplinary improvisation projects. On
 e of her current research focuses is improvisation pedagogy.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260806T031357Z
LOCATION:Äänen Lumo ry\, Nokiantie 2-4\, 00510 Helsinki\, Suomi
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-JAZZFI-SOURCE:gcal
END:VEVENT
