BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuejero - Flamenco-jazz
DTSTART:20260829T160000Z
DTEND:20260829T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260909T123721Z
UID:790bkvspmm5rfhn2ckvm1ifnrm@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260812T120742Z
DESCRIPTION:Vapaa pääsy / Free entry.\n\nCuejero yhdistää flamencon in
 tohimoisen tarinankerronnan pohjoismaisen jazzin sävyihin ja luo omaleima
 isen vuoropuhelun pohjoisen ja etelän välille. Runolliset espanjankielis
 et sanoitukset avautuvat sanojen tuolle puolen improvisaation ja grooven k
 autta. Kulttuurien yhteiselosta ja jaetuilla alueilla syntyneistä musiikk
 iperinteistä ammentava Javier Sánchez Pérezin musiikki tuo yhteen pohjo
 isen intiimit äänimaisemat ja etelän tulisen ilmaisun.\n\nCuejero blend
 s the passionate storytelling of flamenco with Nordic jazz textures in a d
 istinctive dialogue between North and South. Poetic Spanish lyrics move be
 yond words through contemporary improvisation and groove. Inspired by musi
 cal traditions born from the fusion of cultures sharing the same land\, th
 e music of Javier Sánchez Pérez brings together intimate northern sounds
 capes and fiery southern expression.\n\nCuejero combina las texturas del f
 lamenco y del Jazz con improvisaciones enérgicas y ritmos tropicales. Un 
 exquisito cóctel inspirado en el mestizaje entre culturas que comparten u
 na misma tierra. Esta aventura se relata a través del profundo cantar de 
 instrumentos con un pie en la tradición y otro en nuestra sociedad actual
 . Con una poesía musical cautivadora\, Cuejero sumerge al público en un 
 viaje sonoro sin fronteras\, lleno de aventura\, emoción y groove.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T120824Z
LOCATION:El Patio pop-up wine terrace\, Työpajankatu 2a\, 00580 Helsinki\
 , Suomi
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-JAZZFI-SOURCE:gcal
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SOMETHING ELSE vol. 18 | Arola/Salakka/Smith
DTSTART:20260924T160000Z
DTEND:20260924T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260909T123721Z
UID:e916230791171521@facebook.com
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260909T122619Z
DESCRIPTION:Autumn arrives in Helsinki and with it comes an 18th Something
  Else: deep and earthy sound explorations across double bass\, bass clarin
 et\, and cello\, featuring guest artists Jaakko Arola (modified bass clari
 net)\, Aida Salakka (bass\, voice)\, and Wilson Tanner Smith (cello\, flut
 es). Come and gather and cut the crisp evening air with improvised music f
 rom this first-time trio meeting of exciting Helsinki experimentalists.\n\
 nSuggested donation €10-25 (mobilepay or cash)\n2 sets\n7pm\n\nSOMETHING
  ELSE is a concert series for improvised music focused on new meetings of 
 musicians from across Helsinki's free improv\, experimental\, jazz\, elect
 ronic\, and global music scenes\, hosted on the 4th Thursday of each month
  at Kallio's Musta Kissa bar. New small-ensemble groupings--often first-ti
 me meetings--are highlighted each time\, with an emphasis on surprise\, di
 fference\, curiosity\, energy\, and connection.\n\n//\n\nAbout:\n\nJAAKKO 
 AROLA is a musician\, improviser\, composer and instrument-maker from Finl
 and. Arola plays multiple traditional and western woodwind instruments. Hi
 s current practice is centred around expanding the acoustic timbral possib
 ilities of the bass clarinet via a combination of extended techniques and 
 handcrafted mouthpieces.\nhttps://www.jaakkoarola.com/\n\nAIDA SALAKKA is 
 a double bassist\, vocalist and composer based in Helsinki. She works as a
  double bassist in different orchestras and ensembles as well as performs 
 her own solo pieces for her voice and double bass. Aida is currently creat
 ing new solo music for her solo project LOSS\, which is kindly supported b
 y The Swedish Cultural Foundation in Finland.\nhttps://www.instagram.com/a
 kkalasadia/\n\nWILSON TANNER SMITH is a cellist\, composer\, improviser\, 
 and theatre artist currently based in Helsinki. His musical sensibility is
  informed by free improvisation/free jazz\, ambient\, DIY and found sounds
 \, and by many cross-cultural/-genre collaborations in his former hometown
 \, Chicago\, and more recently across northern/western Europe.\nhttps://ww
 w.wilsontannersmith.com\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/916230791171521
 /
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T122657Z
LOCATION:Musta Kissa
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/916230791171521/
X-JAZZFI-SOURCE:gcal
END:VEVENT
