BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kori Jazz The Bridge 2026
DTSTART:20260822T110000Z
DTEND:20260822T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260909T123721Z
UID:1k5j1pive7veo7288oqeg50q48@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260812T113224Z
DESCRIPTION:Livejazzia ja avoimia katukorispelejä! Tule nauttimaan musiik
 ista ja tunnelmasta\, tai hyppää kentälle ja liity mukaan peleihin.\n\n
 Vapaa pääsy!\n\n14.00 Antti Ahoniemi Trio\n15.30 Siina Suutarinen Super 
 Sonic feat. Oona Mattsson\n17.30 Mubba and the Afrotan\n18.45 Open Jam Se
 ssion hosted by Siina Suutarinen Super Sonic\n20.00 Kadi Vija\n\nAntti Aho
 niemi Trio\, established in 2025\, plays mostly original tunes. The trio c
 onstructs lively sets brought to life by the expressiveness of its members
 . Soprano saxophone\, double bass and drums combine with percussions to pr
 ovide an open sound which expands to different directions within the varie
 d tradition of swinging music.\n\nAntti Ahoniemi - double bass\nAdele Saur
 os - soprano saxophone\nJoonas Leppänen - drums\n\nSiina Suutarinen is a 
 singer\, composer and pianist established on the Finnish jazz scene\, now 
 building an international career with her English-language music. Known fo
 r her soft\, distinctive vocal sound — often compared to Diana Krall —
  Suutarinen performs with her band Super Sonic at jazz festivals and clubs
  in Finland and abroad in 2026. At Kori Jazz\, the band's second soloist i
 s saxophonist Oona Mattsson\, bringing her own fresh\, dynamic style. This
  time Suutarinen also plays synth bass\, making this a hybrid lineup you w
 on't want to miss!\n\nSuper Sonic blends vocal-driven jazz with a modern\,
  partly electronic band sound\, aiming to bring jazz closer to audiences a
 nd cross genre lines in an accessible way.\n\nSiina Suutarinen – vocals\
 , synth bass\nOona Mattsson – saxophones\nIlari Mäkelä – piano\, syn
 th\nArttu Huopainen – drums\n\nMubba & The Afrotan is a trans-nation mus
 ic project led by a Tanzanian composer and a bandleader Mubba. The project
  brings together musicians from Africa\, Italy\, Chile and Finland forming
  a live ensemble that reflects the realities of contemporary global cultur
 e. The band fuses Tanzania and broader African rhythms and melodies with j
 azz improvisation developed in Finland creating a new musical expression t
 hrough collaborative composition and performance.\n\nBaraka Issabu - keybo
 ard\, vocal\nJoni Vierre - guitar\nConstanza Garcia - flute\, winds\nHumph
 rey Mubba - bass\, vocal\nAarne Toivonen - drums\n\nSound artist Kadi Vija
  and keyboard player Nikita Rafaelov bring to the stage an intimate and cu
 rious story of family\, love and about looking or seeing in another way. 
 “Tiny Hands Gathering Wonder\, The World Becomes Magic” tells a story 
 of Teppo\, who is born into an LGBTQ+ family – this isn’t childhood fi
 ction but poetry about the mundane\, where the world takes shape from a sl
 ightly different angle. The album\, which won both the Emma and Indie Awar
 d for Jazz of the Year\, was produced by the renowned drummer/producer Tep
 po Mäkynen and was released by the Tampere based Mustik Motel Music in Oc
 tober 2025.\n\nMusically the piece revolves around experimental electronic
  art and indie-style delicateness akin to Radiohead and Björk. The sound 
 is layered and atmospheric – like the thought of a child: a little crook
 ed but right where it should be. On the stage\, Kadi and Nikita create a s
 oundscape where the spectator can listen\, ask\, and be themselves.\n\nKad
 i Vija - synthesizers and vocals\nNikita Rafaelov - synthesizers and keybo
 ards
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T154522Z
LOCATION:Hermannin koripallokenttä\, Hämeentie 105\, 00550 Helsinki\, Su
 omi
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-JAZZFI-SOURCE:gcal
END:VEVENT
